    {
      "data": {
        "content_preview": "**Current State of Open-Weight Coding Models (≈150 words)**  \n\nOpen-weight coding models have advanced rapidly in 2024, achieving performance close to proprietary systems. Meta’s **Code Llama 2**, available up to 70B parameters, leads in scale and achieves around 70% of GPT-4-Turbo’s score on HumanEval, with full model weights accessible. The **StarCoder** series, trained on 2TB of code from The Stack, supports over 50 languages and outperforms earlier open models on MBPP and HumanEval-Plus. **DeepSeek-Coder**, released in March 2024 with 1.3B and 6.7B variants, features instruction tuning and exceeds CodeLlama-7B on programming benchmarks like CodeAlpaca. **CodeMistral-7B** from Mistral AI leverages a curated mix of CodeAlpaca and The Stack, ranking among the top open models on code-specific evaluations. Efficiency improvements now allow quantized and LoRA-finetuned versions to run on consumer GPUs like the RTX 4090, enabling local deployment. Hugging Face’s Open-LLM Leaderboard tracks these developments, reflecting strong community-driven progress in accuracy, language coverage, and accessibility.  \n\nSources: none (live web search unavailable for this run).",
